tests:
  unit:
    count: 15
    covers: "10 new test functions, table-driven rather than one-case-per-fn, over the three files this WU changed (six at the steps, one at the review round, three at step 6). xtask/src/doc.rs (+2): new_surface - a @tier file under ui/src/components/ fires, an untiered collection file does not, a non-test .tsx directly under ui/src/ fires, its .test.tsx does not, a .ts module does not, a Rust file does not; and roster_at over a revision rather than the working tree. xtask/src/gate.rs (+2): over real temp repos - the trigger sees an added component and not its test, its .ts sibling or an untouched component, and an edit and a deletion add no surface; then one red per way a citation breaks (silence on v3, silence on v2 routed to 9·design-schema, an empty list, an unresolvable path, a mismatched blob, a pin too short, a doc that is not a design, an unarchived run) and one green when it all holds; plus components·unbuilt's four answers - unbuilt reds, a blank-reason drop still reds, a drop with a reason greens and is billed as a waiver, a built component owes nothing. xtask/src/notes.rs (+2): absent and empty design.implements parse differently and stay that way, and a drop parses as path + reason with a blank reason being no drop. And the review round added may_be_surface: it must admit every candidate the content test could still accept - a @tier component, an untiered component, a .ts under the collection, a screen - and refuse everything a path alone settles (a module, a test beside either, a nested file, a Rust file, a doc), asserted in both directions because the fix changes WHEN bytes are read and must not change what answer comes back. Step 6 adds three more and extends three. New: doc.rs ui_surface over four paths that render (a root screen, a collection component, and two nested .tsx) and six that do not (a test, a .ts module, a barrel, index.css, a tailwind config, a Rust file), with screen_file separating the collection from everything outside it; gate.rs check_ui_outside_a_wu (Rust and a .ts module are not rendered files, a .tsx in a standalone commit is one refusal under 9\u00b7design); and gate.rs the whole touched half over the same temp repo's SECOND range, where the pill is modified rather than added and another surface is deleted - an unaccounted edit reds and names only the file left standing, a stated reason greens AND lands in report.waived, an empty why reds as its own message, a declaration of a file the diff does not render reds while the real file stays owed. Extended: the added-surface table gains three contradictions (a new surface declared undesigned, a built list naming a file the diff does not render, and a path both cited and declared), the unbuilt test gains a screen design that reds unbuilt and then resolves once ui/src/BodyViewer.tsx exists, and surface_name is asserted on a screen as well as a component. The handoff fixture splits into one repo with two ranges and one test per half, which is also what kept clippy's too_many_lines green without the repo's first #[allow]. The review round adds three more and deletes two. New: added_under over the topology that defeated it - a design added AND removed inside one branch, then merged - which fails without --full-history and passes with it, checked both ways before the flag was kept; surface_at over a real tree, where a nested component, a screen, and a screen carrying a byte no UTF-8 decoder accepts are all surfaces while a barrel, a module and a test are not, and where the roster returns the same four names through the same function; and a rename of a built component, which reads as an added surface and is refused. Deleted: the two tests of new_surface and may_be_surface, whose functions are gone, their content folded into the surface_at and screen_file tests. Review round 2 adds two more. A citation whose bytes do not decode is refused rather than accepted in silence, and the same refusal on a cr/v2 note is tagged 9\u00b7design-schema so the walk can drop it - a note that predates the field is grandfathered through every refusal it can raise, not through all but one. Review round 3 rewrites the rename test rather than adding one: rounds 2 and 3 each caught the rename heuristic exempting a genuinely new surface (a screen scaffolded from deleted filler, then a copy of a live component paired against an unrelated retiring one), so detection is reverted and the test pins the refusal instead - the destination is an added surface, a stated reason does NOT land it, and report.waived stays empty. Totals at this tip: 202 xtask lib tests, all green"
  integration:
    count: 4
    covers: "xtask/tests/dod_gate.rs 66 -> 69, the bounded contract driven through the real binary against temp trees. verify-dod wu reds a tip whose diff adds a @tier component and whose note names no design, and the red names the surface; greens on the same tip with a resolvable citation; and reds a STALE citation - the blob is compared against the tip, not the working tree, so a design edited after the note was written cannot pass. verify-dod epic reds a range that added a component design with no roster entry, stays red with a reasonless drop, greens and bills the reason as a waiver, and needs no record at all once the component lands. Step 6 adds the edit case at the same level: a Working Unit that only re-shapes a screen reds under 9\u00b7design with the file named, then greens once the note declares it undesigned - and the reason prints as a WAIVE line in the report, which is what the epic walk carries up. Totals at this tip: 70 dod_gate tests, all green"
  e2e:
    count: 2
    covers: "NOT WAIVED - this WU's whole exercise, and the epic level the plan refused to defer. xtask/tests/e2e_design_flow.rs 2 -> 4 (--features design-e2e, out of the default suite as the existing flow e2e is): a_build_that_adds_a_surface_cites_the_design_it_read_or_the_merge_refuses_it and a_design_nobody_built_refuses_the_epic_merge_until_the_drop_is_recorded. Step 6 adds two legs to the same tests: a new surface that tries to declare itself undesigned is refused (only a citation answers for one), and a whole edit leg - a Working Unit that re-shapes the screen nobody designed is refused, then lands once its note carries the reason, which the merge prints back. Nine cases over real git through the real merge hook - 12 merges, 7 refused and 5 landed. Each red is bound to its own message (cites no design / cites ... at blob / is a design artifact the design section does not name / components·unbuilt) rather than to a check name, because 9·design is a prefix of 9·design-schema and a bare substring assertion would pass on the wrong red"
