evidence:
  - "the code review found the gate fetching a blob for EVERY added path before any path test, though only the @tier check needs the bytes: measured by its verifier at ~12-14% of a real epic walk's wall time (466 git spawns, 362 of them git show) and ~30% of a single WU gate. may_be_surface now decides from the path and the fetch short-circuits - 8 added paths become 0 fetches on this WU's own seam, and roster_at drops 52 fetches to 26 for the identical reason one caller over"
  - "11 review candidates, one verifier each, 6 refuted - per-surface citation coverage (DEC-25's shape: one family contract spanned seven built components), the registry-oracle parity claim (scoped to membership; the full-contract check exists elsewhere and is stricter), the blob-pin duplication (PIN_MIN and pin_matches are already shared), a second design_run_status parse (only on an already-failing citation, tens of microseconds) and two git spawns per citation (~7ms against a 4.8s walk at 0-1 citations per WU)"
  - "the trigger was measured over the real repository rather than asserted: it fires on 1 seam inside the epic (W5's, 25 surfaces) and produces 0 walk failures, because every seam here carries a cr/v2 note and the walk drops 9·design-schema at seams exactly as DEC-24 already had it. No new discriminator, no cutoff, no walk waiver"
  - "the plan row this refutes was D6·A's premise - 0 of 11 landed UI seams - which measured the epic→main merges on main, seams this epic's walk never re-verifies. Recorded as a deviation rather than quietly re-measured"
  - "components·unbuilt refuses its own author's epic on the first run: 4 of the 20 component designs E-DFLOW wrote have no roster entry, and writing the four reasons found that only one was ever truly unbuilt"
  - "the epic half reads the range's commits (added_under), not the endpoint diff - check 6 forces the same files out of the tree by the epic tip, so an endpoint diff nets an add and a later git rm to nothing"
  - "gate 0 was RED when step 4 began, from step 3: clippy --workspace --all-targets - the exact command gate0.rs runs - refused a 117-line lib test target that step 3's own cargo test never saw. Fixed by shrinking to 91 lines, not by the repo's first #[allow]"
  - "two counts in immutable step records are corrected in the result report: step 4 reported 40 dod_gate tests where the real count at that same commit is 69 (40 is tests/mr.rs), and step 3's seam measurement ran over a local epic/design-flow 21 commits behind its remote - W7's seams were outside the range measured, and the conclusion survives only because W7's single added ui/src path is a test file"
  - "no product code: W8 writes none, and the epic's non-goal holds. The handoff is driven by a fake build - a stub component and a one-line screen - which is the standing risk the plan named at Q2 and W9 pays"
  - "cargo xtask verify-dod epic epic/design-flow --target main, run with the STEP 6 binary over the OLD epic history: 0 failures of any 9·design kind across its 9 seams, and components·unbuilt falls from 4 to 3 because BodyViewer resolves once the roster counts screens. The other 68 failures are the ones the epic already owed - 51 tracked work docs, 8 pre-W8 seams missing notes, 3 open runs, 2 retirement-order, 1 manual review - and none of them moved"
  - "the two blockers the review round found were each REPRODUCED in a scratch repo before an edit, then written as a test run against the unfixed code to watch it fail and against the fixed code to watch it pass. A regression test that passes either way is decoration, and this WU has two that are not"
